{"abstract":"The widespread use of voice-assisted applications using artificial intelligence raises questions about the dynamics of trust and reliance on these systems. While users often rely on these applications for help, instances where users face unforeseen risks and heightened challenges have sparked conversations about the importance of fostering trustworthy artificial intelligence. In this paper, we argue that the prevailing narrative of trust and trustworthiness in relation to artificial intelligence, particularly voice assistants, is misconstrued and fundamentally misplaced. Drawing on insights from philosophy and artificial intelligence literature, we contend that artificial intelligence systems do not meet the criteria for participating in a relationship of trust with human users. Instead, a narrative of reliance is more appropriate. However, we investigate the matter further to explore why the trust/trustworthiness narrative persists, focusing on the unique social dynamics of interactions with voice assistants. We identify factors such as diverse modalities and complexity, social aspects of voice assistants, and issues of uncertainty, assertiveness, and transparency as contributors to the trust narrative. By disentangling these factors, we shed light on the complexities of human-computer interactions and offer insights into the implications for our relationship with artificial intelligence. We advocate for a nuanced understanding of trust and reliance in artificial intelligence systems and provide suggestions for addressing the challenges posed by the dominance of the trust/trustworthiness narrative.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Stamatiou, Filippos","Karakonstantis, Xenofon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765667"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"should you trust your voice assistant it s complicated but no","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp208015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765667","ids":["ku-f099f2d6-81a7-4306-9813-337a915a723f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2EBAB7ED0986787B5CA483586C242950"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp208015","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/409355838/paper_15.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Filippos","key":"stamatioupau","last":"Stamatiou","locid":"3829d616-2e4c-42a6-8167-8ac56a7b1ecf","name":"Stamatiou, Filippos","orcid":"0000-0002-0517-8428","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Florian","key":"westphalpedh","last":"Westphal","name":"Westphal, Florian","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Einav","key":"peretzanderssonpedh","last":"Peretz-Andersson","name":"Peretz-Andersson, Einav","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"riveiropedh","last":"Riveiro","name":"Riveiro, Maria","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kerstin","key":"bachpedh","last":"Bach","name":"Bach, Kerstin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Fredrik","key":"heintzpedh","last":"Heintz","name":"Heintz, Fredrik","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/ecp208015","isbn":["9789180757096"],"issn":["16503740"],"pages":"131-137","series":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings","status":"p","title":"14th Scandinavian Conference on Artificial Intelligence SCAI 2024, June 10-11, 2024, Jönköping, Sweden"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f099f2d6-81a7-4306-9813-337a915a723f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Should You Trust Your Voice Assistant? : It’s Complicated, but No","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765667","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Recent developments in acoustic signal processing have seen the integration of deep learning methodologies, alongside the continued prominence of classical wave expansion-based approaches, particularly in sound field reconstruction. Physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) have emerged as a novel framework, bridging the gap between data-driven and model-based techniques for addressing physical phenomena governed by partial differential equations. This paper introduces a PINN-based approach for the recovery of arbitrary volumetric acoustic fields. The network incorporates the wave equation to impose a regularization on signal reconstruction in the time domain. This methodology enables the network to learn the physical law of sound propagation and allows for the complete characterization of the sound field based on a limited set of observations. The proposed method’s efficacy is validated through experiments involving speech signals in a real-world environment, considering varying numbers of available measurements. Moreover, a comparative analysis is undertaken against state-of-the-art frequency domain and time domain reconstruction methods from existing literature, highlighting the increased accuracy across the various measurement configurations.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Olivieri, Marco","Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Pezzoli, Mirco","Antonacci, Fabio","Sarti, Augusto","Fernandez Grande, Efren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-774941"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Olivieri, Marco"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan"],"keyword":["Physics informed neural network","Sound field reconstruction","Speech signals","Time domain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physics informed neural network for volumetric sound field reconstruction of speech signals","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-024-00366-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-774941","identifier":[{"id":"85203319075","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-083ed9eb-c136-42a8-9860-666282a52e27"],"keyword":["Physics-informed neural network","Sound field reconstruction","Speech signals","Time domain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FFC3AE88A1BB4B0D2689CFD087FDC028"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-024-00366-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/379759389/s13636-024-00366-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Center for Silicon Photonics for Optical Communication (SPOC)","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"olivieripau","last":"Olivieri","name":"Olivieri, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mirco","key":"pezzolipau","last":"Pezzoli","name":"Pezzoli, Mirco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"antonaccipau","last":"Antonacci","name":"Antonacci, Fabio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Augusto","key":"sartipau","last":"Sarti","name":"Sarti, Augusto","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez-Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","name_org":"Fernandez-Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13636-024-00366-2","issn":["16874714","16874722"],"issn_org":["16874714"],"issue":"1","journal":"Eurasip Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing","paperid":"42","publisher":"Springer Open","status":"p","title":"Eurasip Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing","volume":"2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203319075"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-083ed9eb-c136-42a8-9860-666282a52e27"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Physics-informed neural network for volumetric sound field reconstruction of speech signals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-774941","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Immersive spatial audio applications require a detailed understanding of sound fields in large volumes. However, data acquisition is often a restrictive task due to the large number of measurements required. To address this, we propose a Bayesian framework for Room Impulse Response reconstruction from a set of limited measurements. This approach enables the inclusion of physically-grounded models and explicit regularisation based on generalisable room properties in the frequency domain. Evaluation via experimental measurements in a historical academic auditorium demonstrates an efficient and accurate reconstruction, indicating potential applications in navigable sound field reproduction and augmented reality spatial audio.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Figueroa Durán, Antonio Andrés","Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Fernandez Grande, Efren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759055"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-17","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2024-06-15","title":"AES 156<sup>th Convention</sup>","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bayesian framework for room impulse response reconstruction using explicit frequency regularisation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-759055","ids":["dtu-53da7b7e-c124-4302-9b7f-4a801dfce68b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0B0A50DDA076F5B2A8E0F46216505862"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonio Andrés","key":"figueroaduránpau","last":"Figueroa Durán","locid":"b7e566a2-bec3-4eaf-875c-515a258c8caa","name":"Figueroa Durán, Antonio Andrés","orcid":"0000-0001-6419-6418","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Audio Engineering Society","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of AES 156<sup>th</sup> Convention"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-53da7b7e-c124-4302-9b7f-4a801dfce68b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Bayesian Framework for Room Impulse Response Reconstruction using Explicit Frequency Regularisation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759055","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"A method is presented for estimating and reconstructing the sound field within a room using physics-informed neural networks. By incorporating a limited set of experimental room impulse responses as training data, this approach combines neural network processing capabilities with the underlying physics of sound propagation, as articulated by the wave equation. The network's ability to estimate particle velocity and intensity, in addition to sound pressure, demonstrates its capacity to represent the flow of acoustic energy and completely characterise the sound field with only a few measurements. Additionally, an investigation into the potential of this network as a tool for improving acoustic simulations is conducted. This is due to its proficiency in offering grid-free sound field mappings with minimal inference time. Furthermore, a study is carried out which encompasses comparative analyses against current approaches for sound field reconstruction. Specifically, the proposed approach is evaluated against both data-driven techniques and elementary wave-based regression methods. The results demonstrate that the physics-informed neural network stands out when reconstructing the early part of the room impulse response, while simultaneously allowing for complete sound field characterisation in the time domain.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Caviedes Nozal, Diego","Richard, Antoine Philippe André","Fernandez Grande, Efren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718667"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"room impulse response reconstruction with physics informed deep learning","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/352477126/1048_1_10.0024750.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718667","identifier":[{"id":"38341739","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184994972","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a3cf3223-bef8-45ab-acdf-60eea89d5d27"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D8EBEF5717F25041E39FF3549A1B268"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/352477126/1048_1_10.0024750.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diego","key":"caviedesnozalpau","last":"Caviedes-Nozal","locid":"49ee27ef-8c53-4d9b-9588-9484f01c214a","name":"Caviedes Nozal, Diego","name_org":"Caviedes-Nozal, Diego","orcid":"0000-0001-6756-3375","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Antoine","key":"richardpau","last":"Richard","locid":"1707a037-d2fe-48e5-aebf-7388901b1666","name":"Richard, Antoine Philippe André","name_org":"Richard, Antoine","orcid":"0000-0002-4171-7599","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez-Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","name_org":"Fernandez-Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38341739"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1121/10.0024750","issn":["00014966","01630962"],"issn_org":["00014966"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","pages":"1048-1059","publisher":"Acoustical Society of America","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","volume":"155"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184994972"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a3cf3223-bef8-45ab-acdf-60eea89d5d27"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Room impulse response reconstruction with physics-informed deep learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718667","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The practice of reconstructing sound fields from spatial measurements stands at the crossroads of physics, data science, and auditory science. Since the proliferation of spatial audio technology, there is an increasing need for efficient algorithms capable of reconstructing sound fields. Despite critical applications in virtual reality, architectural acoustics, and noise control, the discipline faces significant challenges, chiefly due to the intricate nature of sound propagation and the limitations of spatial sampling methods. Conventional approaches to sound field reconstruction, although foundational, often face these limitations in challenging acoustic environments. On the other hand, deep learning is adept at identifying patterns within data. However, spatially sampled signals often lack the structure that neural networks require for effective processing. This gap highlights the necessity for integrating the physics of wave propagation and other relevant inductive biases into deep learning models to aid in analysing sound fields. This Ph.D. thesis delves into the frontier of data-driven methods for sound field analysis and reconstruction, with a focus on using deep learning to transcend these limitations. Central to this exploration is the development of generative models that adhere to the principles of acoustic wave propagation, physics-informed neural networks constrained by the wave equation for acoustic field characterisation, and (iii) rotational equivariance constraints for convolutional neural networks, adapted for spherical microphone array processing. Generative models have the capacity to capture the complexities of high-dimensional data distributions. Despite their significant appetite for data, it is shown that they can be effectively primed with the statistical properties of sound fields using Monte Carlo simulations, thereby serving as a powerful prior for tackling inverse problems in acoustics of lightly damped enclosures and improving the reconstruction quality over other state-of-the-art approaches. Furthermore, they can offer insight into the uncertainty of measuring, reconstructing, and analysing acoustic pressurefields. Physics-informed neural networks offer a fusion of physical principles and parameter estimation. These networks can embed the governing equations of acoustics directly into the architecture of deep learning models. This integration allows them to not only learn from data but also respect the underlying physics of sound propagation. They are shown to perform well in both room impulse response reconstruction and spatiotemporal speech signal reconstruction tasks, as well as provide a means for efficient and complete characterisation of sound fields in the time domain. Finally, it is shown that combining convolutional neural networks with rotational equivariance can benefit source localisation tasks when using spherical microphone arrays. The adaptation of neural networks to respect this symmetry can assist in robustness to variations in microphone array orientation but also more aligned with the geometrical properties of an acoustic environment. This dissertation aims to explore and analyse the significant findings and evaluate the contributions of the Ph.D. study within the context of the current state of knowledge. ","author_count":1,"contributors":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764425"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acoustic holography","Deep learning","Microphone array","Reverberant sound field","Sound field reconstruction","Source localisation","Spatial sampling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data driven methods for large scale sound field acquisition and analysis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dtp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376041900/PhD_thesis_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764425","ids":["dtu-d23e1712-150a-47cf-82f2-d6e64cee0707"],"keyword":["Acoustic holography","Deep learning","Inductive bias","Microphone array","Reverberant sound field","Sound field reconstruction","Source localisation","Spatial sampling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CB7E8D15A4B043AD33DFE7F59CF24CEB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376041900/PhD_thesis_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"220","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d23e1712-150a-47cf-82f2-d6e64cee0707"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Data-driven methods for large-scale sound field acquisition and analysis","type":"Thesis PhD","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764425","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a deep learning-based approach for the spatiotemporal reconstruction of sound fields using generative adversarial networks. The method utilises a plane wave basis and learns the underlying statistical distributions of pressure in rooms to accurately reconstruct sound fields from a limited number of measurements. The performance of the method is evaluated using two established datasets and compared to state-of-the-art methods. The results show that the model is able to achieve an improved reconstruction performance in terms of accuracy and energy retention, particularly in the high-frequency range and when extrapolating beyond the measurement region. Furthermore, the proposed method can handle a varying number of measurement positions and configurations without sacrificing performance. The results suggest that this approach provides a promising approach to sound field reconstruction using generative models that allow for a physically informed prior to acoustics problems.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Fernandez Grande, Efren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-688792"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generative adversarial networks with physical sound field priors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333879337/1226_1_10.0020665.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-688792","identifier":[{"id":"85168610863","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37615413","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-3f3a4952-e85a-403a-b2a1-67866b81c36e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16CEA2C711837E8AF469B3DFF9E1A508"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333879337/1226_1_10.0020665.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez-Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","name_org":"Fernandez-Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37615413"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1121/10.0020665","issn":["00014966","01630962"],"issn_org":["00014966"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","pages":"1226-1238","publisher":"Acoustical Society of America","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","volume":"154"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168610863"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3f3a4952-e85a-403a-b2a1-67866b81c36e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Generative adversarial networks with physical sound field priors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-688792","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Over the last couple of decades, sound field analysis and reconstruction methods have enabled us to observe and better understand diverse acoustic phenomena, from jetnoise to the sound of historical violins. In a broad sense, sound field reconstruction methods consist of capturing the spatial properties of sound, in order to visualize, analyze, reproduce, or manipulate the sound field in various ways. Fueled by advances in instrumentation and signal processing, these methods have had a profound impact in the field of acoustics and have been widely adopted in areas like vibro-acoustics, spatial audio, room acoustics, materials and electroacoustics – among others. In this talk we discuss new approaches for capturing and reconstructing sound fields in space, motivated by some of the longstanding challenges in the field. Specifically, we consider: 1) novel sensing methods, with a focus on optical remote sensing and the acousto-optic interaction, to measure sound using light, 2) physical models for largescale sound field visualization/reconstruction and 3) Deep Learning approaches for augmenting conventional acoustic measurements. Finally, we share an outlook of this multifaceted and increasingly relevant domain of acoustics.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fernandez Grande, Efren","Verburg Riezu, Samuel Arturo","Karakonstantis, Xenofon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689165"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-15","place":"Torino, it","start":"2023-09-11","title":"10th Convention of the European Acoustics Association","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acoustic holography","Measurement techniques","Room acoustics","Signal processing","Sound field analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sound field reconstruction towards large scale spatial sensing","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/335945829/Forum_Acusticum_E_Fernandez-Grande-final.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689165","ids":["dtu-fd75c931-c778-4a90-b80d-e238bcd33b04"],"keyword":["Acoustic holography","Measurement techniques","Room acoustics","Signal processing","Sound field analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5B92EF64FF5FE5823E61E0DE6F471FF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/335945829/Forum_Acusticum_E_Fernandez-Grande-final.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Arturo","key":"verburgriezupau","last":"Verburg Riezu","locid":"3003e342-662b-47cf-a000-df3ffd8ed0d0","name":"Verburg Riezu, Samuel Arturo","orcid":"0000-0003-2895-2946","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fd75c931-c778-4a90-b80d-e238bcd33b04"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Sound field reconstruction: towards large-scale spatial sensing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689165","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present a method for reconstructing the sound field in a room using physics-informed neural networks. Our approach employs a limited set of room impulse responses as training data for the network, while also incorporating the fundamental physical principles of sound propagation in space through the use of the wave equation. This allows the network to not only learn the underlying physics of sound propagation but also utilize the nonlinear mapping capabilities of neural networks to adjust for any inhomogeneities in the room and measurement artifacts. Furthermore, the network can determine particle velocity and intensity through the use of autodifferentiation. The results indicate the effectiveness of the approach in terms of reconstruction accuracy and computational efficiency. This work presents a promising approach for sound field reconstruction and has potential for improving the representation of sound fields in various acoustic settings, including rooms and other complex environments, particularly for the synthesis of room impulse responses.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Fernandez Grande, Efren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700793"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-15","place":"Torino, it","start":"2023-09-11","title":"10th Convention of the European Acoustics Association","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon"],"keyword":["Deep learning","Physics informed neural network"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"room impulse response reconstruction using physics constrained neural networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/340296554/PINNs_Forum_Acusticum1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700793","ids":["dtu-35826ef5-0bff-4b5e-9415-c8611170119d"],"keyword":["Deep learning","Physics-informed neural network","Room impulse responses","Sound field"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-24BCD213BC95E334EE3F3F25BAB1CBFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/340296554/PINNs_Forum_Acusticum1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"European Acoustics Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 10<sup>th</sup> Convention of the European Acoustics Association"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-35826ef5-0bff-4b5e-9415-c8611170119d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Room Impulse response reconstruction using physics-constrained neural networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700793","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This work examines the use of generative adversarial networks for reconstructing sound fields from experimental data. It is investigated whether generative models, which learn the underlying statistics of a given signal or process, can improve the spatio-temporal reconstruction of a sound field by extending its bandwidth. The problem is significant as acoustic array processing is naturally band limited by the spatial sampling of the sound field (due to the difficulty to satisfy the Nyquist criterion in space domain at high frequencies). In this study, the reconstruction of spatial room impulse responses in a conventional room is tested based on three different generative adversarial models. The results indicate that the models can improve the reconstruction, mostly by recovering some of the sound field energy that would otherwise be lost at high frequencies. There is an encouraging outlook in the use of statistical learning models to overcome the bandwidth limitations of acoustic sensor arrays. The approach can be of interest in other areas, such as computational acoustics, to alleviate the classical computational burden at high frequencies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fernandez Grande, Efren","Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Caviedes Nozal, Diego","Gerstoft, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669539"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at San Diego"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generative models for sound field reconstruction","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0016896","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the VILLUM Foundation under Grant No. 19179, “Large-scale acoustic holography.” The authors would like to thank Samuel A. Verburg, Herbert Groll, Mike Bianco, and the team at Noise-Lab [Scripps, University of California San Diego (UCSD)] for valuable help at the early stages of this work. Codes for the GAN models of this paper are made available at https://github.com/xefonon/BandwidthExtensionRIRs . This work was supported by the VILLUM Foundation under Grant No. 19179, “Large-scale acoustic holography.” The authors would like to thank Samuel A. Verburg, Herbert Groll, Mike Bianco, and the team at Noise-Lab [Scripps, University of California San Diego (UCSD)] for valuable help at the early stages of this work. Codes for the GAN models of this paper are made available at https://github.com/xefonon/BandwidthExtensionRIRs."],"id":"S01-000.00-669539","identifier":[{"id":"36859132","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85148422919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f87786d5-602b-4aa7-ad6d-f0555986312c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-40DBBC9C770D2B51A77A87F606D0B42F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0016896","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/318643462/1179_1_online.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at san diego","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at San Diego","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez-Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","name_org":"Fernandez-Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diego","key":"caviedesnozalpau","last":"Caviedes-Nozal","locid":"49ee27ef-8c53-4d9b-9588-9484f01c214a","name":"Caviedes Nozal, Diego","name_org":"Caviedes-Nozal, Diego","orcid":"0000-0001-6756-3375","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"gerstoftpau","last":"Gerstoft","name":"Gerstoft, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36859132"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1121/10.0016896","issn":["00014966","01630962"],"issn_org":["00014966"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","pages":"1179-1190","publisher":"Acoustical Society of America","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148422919"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f87786d5-602b-4aa7-ad6d-f0555986312c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Generative models for sound field reconstruction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669539","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Spherical microphone arrays enable the directional decomposition of a sound field over all propagation angles and are therefore a valuable analysis tool in enclosures. At the same time, deep neural networks have shown promising performance in acoustic source localisation tasks, especially in challenging acoustic scenarios. Combining neural network source localisation with spherical array signals can prove extremely beneficial in existent applications. However, classical neural networks typically exploit one- or two-dimensional data correlations. This can cause the network estimation to be prone to errors in wave propagation direction and limiting the array to specific directions, since the network does not guarantee rotational invariance. In this study, we examine a spherical graph neural network architecture for direction of arrival estimation trained on both simulated and measured sound field features. The spherical graph neural network can capture spherical correlations and can warrant that they are held approximately invariant for rotations. The networks’ performance is preliminarily investigated under anechoic conditions with the respective measured spherical array impulse responses.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Fernandez Grande, Efren","Hahmann, Manuel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380934"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-28","place":"Gyeongju, kr","start":"2022-10-24","title":"24<sup>th</sup> International Congress on Acoustics","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Direction of arrival","Machine learning","Neural network","Spherical microphone array"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"localising acoustic sources with a spherical graph neural network","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85192519388","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380934","identifier":[{"id":"85192519388","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ff0f611c-3fdd-488b-bc8d-04933a00e02c"],"keyword":["Direction of arrival","Machine learning","Neural network","Spherical microphone array"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C17616C3EE47DBA10D1E6F9B3C7E1F05"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuel","key":"hahmannpau","last":"Hahmann","locid":"a3b63872-eb2f-40fb-ac06-11541ed33d23","name":"Hahmann, Manuel","orcid":"0000-0001-7325-3584","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 24<sup>th</sup> International Congress on Acoustics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ff0f611c-3fdd-488b-bc8d-04933a00e02c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Localising acoustic sources with a spherical graph neural network","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380934","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The characterisation of Room Impulse Responses over an extended region in a room by means of measurements requires dense spatial sampling with many microphones. This can often become intractable and time-consuming in practice. Well established reconstruction methods such as plane wave regression show that the sound field in a room can be reconstructed from sparsely distributed measurements. However, these reconstructions usually rely on assuming physical sparsity (i.e. few waves compose the sound field) or trait in the measured sound field, making the models less generalisable and problem-specific. In this paper, we introduce a method to reconstruct a sound field in an enclosure with the use of a Generative Adversarial Network (GAN), which synthesises new variants of the data distributions that it is trained upon. The proposed GAN model aims to estimate the underlying distribution of plane waves in any source free region and map these distributions from a stochastic, latent representation. A GAN is trained on a large number of synthesised sound fields represented by a random wave field and then tested on simulated sets of reverberant rooms.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Fernandez Grande, Efren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316370"],"event":{"end":"2021-08-05","place":"Washington, us","start":"2021-08-01","title":"50<sup>th</sup> International Congress and Expo on Noise Control Engineering","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sound field reconstruction in rooms with deep generative models","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85117391998","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316370","identifier":[{"id":"85117391998","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-27ac33dd-0e4c-46b1-8d01-3bf4fcf3b709"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B6C3B9C3FD4F2FBBE9A5926AE1B4B003"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3397/in-2021-1864","pages":"1527-1538","publisher":"Institute of Noise Control Engineering","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of INTER-NOISE 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117391998"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-27ac33dd-0e4c-46b1-8d01-3bf4fcf3b709"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Sound field reconstruction in rooms with deep generative models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316370","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The acquisition of the spatio-temporal characteristics of a sound field over a large volume of space is experimentally challenging, as a large number of transducers is required to sample the sound field. Sound field reconstruction methods are a resourceful approach, as they enable the interpolation and extrapolation of the sound field from a limited number of observed data. In this study we examine the spatio-temporal and spatio-spectral reconstruction of the sound field in a room from distributed measurements of the sound pressure. Specifically, a variational Gaussian process regression model is formulated, using time-domain anisotropic kernels to reconstruct the direct sound and early reflections, and frequency-domain isotropic kernels for reconstructing the late reverberant field. The proposed methodology is compared experimentally to classical regression models based on plane wave decompositions, which are widely used in sound field reconstruction in enclosures due to their simplicity and accuracy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fernandez Grande, Efren","Caviedes Nozal, Diego","Hahmann, Manuel","Karakonstantis, Xenofon","Verburg Riezu, Samuel Arturo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-314629"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-10","place":"Bologna, it","start":"2021-09-08","title":"International Conference on Immersive and 3D Audio<br/>","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["6DOF","Acoustic holography","Gaussian processes","Microphone arrays","Room impulse response","Sound field reconstruction","Spatial audio"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconstruction of room impulse responses over extended domains for navigable sound field reproduction","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258847187/i3da_2021_paper_63_R1_OK.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-314629","identifier":[{"id":"85123203896","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-21d15cd1-c17c-4c66-a6bd-41f7d114c11e"],"keyword":["6dof","Acoustic holography","Gaussian processes","Microphone arrays","Room impulse response","Sound field reconstruction","Spatial audio"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F0E559C08985D78415A212DC82629F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258847187/i3da_2021_paper_63_R1_OK.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Acoustic Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Efren","key":"fernandezgrandepau","last":"Fernandez Grande","locid":"f3251df1-9730-455a-9a5d-97e2a6128e79","name":"Fernandez Grande, Efren","orcid":"0000-0002-8900-183X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diego Caviedes","key":"nozalpau","last":"Nozal","locid":"49ee27ef-8c53-4d9b-9588-9484f01c214a","name":"Caviedes Nozal, Diego","name_org":"Nozal, Diego Caviedes","orcid":"0000-0001-6756-3375","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuel","key":"hahmannpau","last":"Hahmann","locid":"a3b63872-eb2f-40fb-ac06-11541ed33d23","name":"Hahmann, Manuel","orcid":"0000-0001-7325-3584","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xenofon","key":"karakonstantispau","last":"Karakonstantis","locid":"26412133-5e12-40a2-abe9-a1907742eb6f","name":"Karakonstantis, Xenofon","orcid":"0000-0001-6810-2028","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuel Arturo","key":"verburgriezupau","last":"Verburg Riezu","locid":"3003e342-662b-47cf-a000-df3ffd8ed0d0","name":"Verburg Riezu, Samuel Arturo","orcid":"0000-0003-2895-2946","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/i3da48870.2021.9610846","isbn":["9781665409988"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of International Conference on Immersive and 3D Audio"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123203896"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-21d15cd1-c17c-4c66-a6bd-41f7d114c11e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Reconstruction of room impulse responses over extended domains for navigable sound field reproduction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-314629","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
